prompt:
In the state machine `fsm`, states 2 and 3 are terminal. Add to the postcondition of `fsm::step` that a terminal state never changes, keeping everything else.

Required signature (in unit `fsm`):
fn step(s: i64, ev: i64) -> (r: i64)

reference.code:
spec fn sticky(s: i64, r: i64) -> bool { (s == 2 || s == 3) ==> r == s }

#[effects(pure)]
#[uses(state_ok, sticky)]
fn step(s: i64, ev: i64) -> (r: i64)
    requires state_ok(s),
    ensures state_ok(r), sticky(s, r),
{
    if s == 0 {
        if ev == 1 {
            1
        } else {
            0
        }
    } else {
        if s == 1 {
            if ev == 2 {
                2
            } else {
                if ev < 0 {
                    3
                } else {
                    1
                }
            }
        } else {
            s
        }
    }
}
